# Zenith Anti-AI-Slop UI & Clean Architecture Rules

Authored by **Sarvesh Zenith** (*Sarvesh Khandelwal / Dayal Infotech Services*).

## UI/UX & Code Quality Guidelines
- **Anti-AI-Slop Code Standard**: Avoid boilerplate-heavy, redundant, or overly repetitive generative AI code patterns. Keep component structures concise, idiomatic, and highly maintainable.
- **Clean Architecture & Separation of Concerns**:
  - Keep UI components visual and presentation-focused.
  - Decouple business logic, state management, and API integrations into dedicated hooks/services.
- **Performance & Design System Discipline**:
  - Prefer modern CSS/Tailwind utilities over bloated inline styling.
  - Implement strict error boundaries and accessible, responsive design patterns.

